For a production MinIO server, the recommended approach is not to configure SSL directly inside MinIO. Instead, use Nginx as a reverse proxy with a Let's Encrypt certificate.

Recommended architecture:

Internet
     │
     ▼
HTTPS (443)
     │
     ▼
Nginx
     │
     ├──> MinIO API (9500)
     │
     └──> MinIO Console (9501)

This gives you:

✅ Free Let's Encrypt SSL certificates
✅ Automatic certificate renewal
✅ Better security
✅ Easier management
✅ Standard production deployment
Step 1: Configure DNS

Create DNS records:

Type	Host	Points To
A	storage	YOUR_PUBLIC_IP
A	console	YOUR_PUBLIC_IP

Example:

storage.example.com
console.example.com
Step 2: Install Nginx
sudo apt update
sudo apt install nginx -y

Enable it:

sudo systemctl enable nginx
sudo systemctl start nginx
Step 3: Create an Nginx configuration
sudo nano /etc/nginx/sites-available/minio

Example:

server {
    listen 80;
    server_name storage.example.com;

    location / {
        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:9500;

        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto https;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
    }
}

server {
    listen 80;
    server_name console.example.com;

    location / {
        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:9501;

        proxy_http_version 1.1;

        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
        proxy_set_header Connection "upgrade";

        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto https;
    }
}

Enable it:

sudo ln -s /etc/nginx/sites-available/minio /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/
sudo nginx -t
sudo systemctl reload nginx
Step 4: Install Certbot
sudo apt install certbot python3-certbot-nginx -y
Step 5: Obtain SSL certificates
sudo certbot --nginx

Select:

storage.example.com
console.example.com

Certbot will automatically:

Install the certificates
Configure HTTPS
Redirect HTTP to HTTPS
Step 6: Update the MinIO configuration

Edit:

sudo nano /etc/default/minio

Update:

MINIO_SERVER_URL="https://storage.example.com"

Restart MinIO:

sudo systemctl restart minio
Step 7: Verify

Open:

https://storage.example.com

API endpoint:

https://storage.example.com

Console:

https://console.example.com
